			"id":"2bf511efd69a5fab",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n\n\n# 1. Meeting objective\n\n> **The main objective today is to align on the minimum API scope required for PPJ to build the GDI automation interface, and to understand the existing WFX business rules before we finalize the API payload design.**\n\n3 kết quả cần đạt cuối buổi:\n\n1. WFX xác nhận API nào hiện đã có / cần develop.\n2. Chốt nguyên tắc **1 FPO → 1 GDI hay multi-FPO → 1 GDI**.\n3. Chốt minimum request/response fields để PPJ bắt đầu build UI.\n\n# 2. Opening script\n\n> Hi Ankur, Anupam and team. Thanks for arranging the discussion.\n>\n> Today, we would like to keep the discussion quite practical and simple.\n>\n> PPJ has not yet built the automation tool, so the JSON structures in our document should be considered conceptual rather than fixed technical requirements.\n>\n> Our main objective is first to understand what WFX can provide through supported APIs, and then we will design our UI and integration layer around the available WFX capabilities.\n\n# 3. Explain the initiative\n\n> Currently, our users perform the Common GDI for FPO process manually in WFX.\n>\n> They need to search for the relevant OC, Style, Production Order or FPO, select the correct site and Linked Store, load Material Allocation information, select the required materials and quantities, and then Issue the GDI.\n>\n> After that, they still need to search for the generated GDI number and maintain separate tracking outside WFX.\n>\n> PPJ would therefore like to build a simplified internal automation interface.\n\nTarget flow:\n\n```text\nPPJ User\n   ↓\nPPJ Automation UI\n   ↓\nPPJ Integration Layer\n   ↓\nWFX APIs\n   ↓\nWFX creates official GDI\n   ↓\nGDI No. + Status returned to PPJ\n```\n\nQuan trọng phải nói:\n\n> PPJ will build the UI and workflow orchestration.\n>\n> We are not requesting WFX to develop another user interface.\n>\n> What we need from WFX is the supported API layer for fetching, validating, creating and retrieving GDI-related transactions.\n\n# 4. API scope cần WFX support\n\nNên gom lại thành **4 API capability groups**, không nên list 15–20 APIs trong meeting.\n\n| Capability | PPJ cần gì |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Search / Fetch | OC, Style, PO/FPO, Material Allocation, Indent, Article, Qty |\n| 2. Master / Context | Company, Branch, Site, Linked Store, Category, Product Group |\n| 3. Validate / Create | Validate quantity + create Common GDI for FPO |\n| 4. Result / Tracking | GDI ID, GDI No., status, error, transaction details |\n\nScript:\n\n> From our perspective, we can simplify the requirement into four capability groups: search and fetch, master-data context, validation and GDI creation, and finally result/status retrieval.\n>\n> We are flexible regarding whether WFX exposes these as four APIs, multiple APIs, or an existing standard interface.\n\n# 5. Batch ID clarification\n\nĐây là điểm Ankur đang hỏi nhiều, nên chủ động đơn giản hóa.\n\nNói thẳng:\n\n> Regarding Batch ID, we do not consider it a mandatory WFX concept.\n>\n> Batch ID would mainly be an internal PPJ reference if our UI allows users to submit several requests together.\n>\n> WFX does not necessarily need to understand or process the Batch ID.\n\nNên chốt identifier như sau:\n\n| ID | Owner | Requirement |\n|---|---|---|\n| `batchId` | PPJ | Optional |\n| `requestRowId` | PPJ | Optional |\n| `clientRequestId` | PPJ → WFX | Recommended |\n| `gdiId` | WFX | Required response |\n| `gdiNo` | WFX | Required response |\n\nScript:\n\n> The only external reference that we think is useful is a `clientRequestId`, mainly for duplicate prevention and retry handling.\n>\n> WFX would then return the generated `gdiId` and `gdiNo`.\n\n# 6. Biggest business question: one FPO or multiple FPOs?\n\nĐừng nói rằng PPJ yêu cầu 1 FPO = 1 GDI.\n\nHãy hỏi WFX business rule trước.\n\n> One important point we would like WFX to clarify is whether Common GDI for FPO currently requires one GDI per FPO.\n>\n> We do not want to introduce this restriction from the PPJ side if WFX itself does not require it.\n\nCác câu hỏi:\n\n1. Can one GDI contain multiple FPOs?\n2. If yes, under what conditions?\n3. Must they have the same:\n   - OC?\n   - Style?\n   - Site?\n   - Linked Store?\n   - Category?\n   - Warehouse?\n4. What condition forces WFX to split them into separate GDIs?\n\nSau đó:\n\n> For Phase 1, if one FPO per request is simpler and aligns with WFX business rules, PPJ is completely fine with that.\n>\n> We prefer the simplest supported transaction model.\n\n# 7. JSON design: keep it minimal\n\nKhông nên ngồi mapping 50 fields hôm nay.\n\nĐề xuất conceptual request:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"clientRequestId\": \"PPJ-GDI-000001\",\n  \"company\": \"...\",\n  \"branch\": \"...\",\n  \"fpoNo\": \"...\",\n  \"fromSite\": \"...\",\n  \"linkedStore\": \"...\",\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"materialLineId\": \"...\",\n      \"issueQty\": 100\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nResponse:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"clientRequestId\": \"PPJ-GDI-000001\",\n  \"gdiId\": \"...\",\n  \"gdiNo\": \"...\",\n  \"status\": \"CREATED\",\n  \"errors\": []\n}\n```\n\nVà nói:\n\n> This is only an illustrative structure.\n>\n> We would actually prefer WFX to recommend the minimum mandatory header and line-level fields based on the existing Common GDI for FPO transaction.\n\nĐiều này rất quan trọng: **đẩy source-of-truth technical mapping về phía WFX**, vì họ hiểu transaction engine của họ nhất.\n\n# 8. Quantity logic cần clarify\n\nCó hai trường hợp business:\n\n### Full issue\n\n```text\nIssue Qty = Current Open Qty\n```\n\n### Partial issue\n\n```text\nIssue Qty = User-entered Qty\n```\n\nHỏi WFX:\n\n> Can WFX expose the current open quantity and maximum issuable quantity through API?\n>\n> And during GDI creation, can WFX perform the final stock and open-quantity validation again?\n\nPPJ không nên tự calculate.\n\n# 9. Material filtering\n\nPPJ UI có thể cho user chọn:\n\n- OC / Style / FPO\n- Linked Store\n- Category\n- Product Group\n- Sub Category — optional\n- Article — optional\n\nNhưng logic eligibility phải từ WFX.\n\nScript:\n\n> PPJ may provide filtering controls in our UI, but the eligible material lines should always come from WFX.\n>\n> We do not want PPJ to independently recreate WFX allocation or inventory rules.\n\n# 10. Error handling\n\nKhông cần thiết kế error framework phức tạp.\n\nChỉ cần yêu cầu:\n\n```text\nSUCCESS\nVALIDATION_ERROR\nFAILED\n```\n\nvà:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"code\": \"INSUFFICIENT_STOCK\",\n  \"message\": \"Available quantity is lower than requested quantity\",\n  \"lineId\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\nNói:\n\n> We only need errors to be clear enough for the user to understand which transaction or material line failed and why.\n\n# 11. Questions cần WFX trả lời trong meeting\n\nCó thể dùng nguyên list này:\n\n### API Availability\n\n1. Which existing APIs can support Common GDI for FPO?\n2. Which capabilities require new development?\n3. Is there already an API for Material Allocation / Adhoc Indent?\n4. Is there an API for official GDI creation?\n5. Can the API return the GDI number immediately?\n\n### Business Rules\n\n6. Can one GDI contain multiple FPOs?\n7. What conditions require GDI splitting?\n8. Can Full Open and Partial Issue both be supported?\n9. What validation is performed when the user clicks Issue today?\n10. Can these same validations be executed through API?\n\n### Data\n\n11. What are the mandatory header fields?\n12. What are the mandatory line fields?\n13. Which unique WFX IDs should PPJ use for Material Allocation / Indent lines?\n\n### Technical\n\n14. What authentication method should PPJ use?\n15. Is a UAT environment available?\n16. How should duplicate requests be prevented?\n17. What is the expected timeline if API development is required?\n\n# 12. Things NOT to finalize today\n\nKhông cần tranh luận sâu về:\n\n- final JSON schema;\n- Batch ID structure;\n- internal PPJ database;\n- UI screen design;\n- DWH schema;\n- batch orchestration;\n- 50 vs 100 concurrent requests;\n- multi-FPO payload;\n- detailed status model.\n\nNói:\n\n> Once the available WFX APIs and transaction rules are confirmed, PPJ can finalize these technical details internally.\n\n# 13. Recommended decision at the end\n\nMeeting nên kết thúc bằng matrix:\n\n| Item | Decision needed |\n|---|---|\n| Existing APIs | Available / Not available |\n| Material Allocation API | Yes / New development |\n| GDI Create API | Yes / New development |\n| One vs Multiple FPO | WFX rule |\n| Full / Partial Issue | Supported / Not supported |\n| Client Request ID | Supported / Alternative |\n| GDI status retrieval | API available? |\n| UAT | Environment + access |\n| WFX action | API spec / estimate |\n| PPJ action | UI + mapping after API confirmation |\n\n# 14. Closing script\n\n> Thanks, everyone.\n>\n> From PPJ's side, we would like to keep Phase 1 as simple as possible.\n>\n> Our priority is not to define a complicated batch or JSON framework at this stage. We first need a supported way to retrieve the required WFX data, submit a valid Common GDI for FPO transaction, receive the generated GDI number, and check its status.\n>\n> Once WFX confirms the available APIs and business rules, PPJ will adapt our automation UI and integration design accordingly.\n>\n> After today's discussion, we can update the SRS with the agreed API scope and move forward with the detailed field mapping.\n\n## 15. Một câu nên dùng xuyên suốt meeting\n\nNếu discussion bắt đầu đi quá sâu vào technical JSON, quay lại câu này:\n\n> **Since PPJ has not built the automation application yet, we would prefer to align with the existing WFX transaction model rather than define a new technical model upfront.**\n\nĐây nên là **key positioning của buổi meeting hôm nay**.",
